note Exercism-style exercise "prime-factors": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/prime-factors
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note factors writes the prime factors of value into o, smallest first and with repetition, and
note returns how many it wrote.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/prime-factors
om2
fn factors value ulong o edit ulong * to ulong
n = value
k = ulong 0
d = ulong 2
while le mul d d n bound 999999
if eq rem n d 0
put o k d
k = add k 1
n = div n d
else
d = add d 1
end
end
if gt n 1
put o k n
k = add k 1
end
ret k
end
